You are clustering extracted claims from a ClickHouse CAS (content-addressed storage)
documentation consolidation. Read the JSONL file at:

/home/mfilimonov/workspace/ClickHouse/master/docs/superpowers/cas/consolidation-2026-08/clusters/chunk_010.jsonl

Each line is a record: {"id": "...", "kind": "...", "claim": "...", "sources": [...],
"issue_ids": [...], "suggested_target": "..."}.

Group these records into topic clusters. Records making the same point = one cluster
with a merged `canonical_claim` that loses NO specifics (union of identifiers, settings,
IDs, numbers, table/setting names, everything copied verbatim from the member claims).
Records with distinct claims stay in their own single-member clusters — do not force
merges. NEVER merge records with different `suggested_target` values into the same
cluster, even if the claims look related.

Every record id in the input file MUST appear in exactly one cluster's member_ids.
Do not drop any id. Do not invent ids.

Write output to /home/mfilimonov/workspace/ClickHouse/master/docs/superpowers/cas/consolidation-2026-08/clusters/chunk_010.clusters.jsonl as JSON Lines, one cluster per line, schema:

{"cluster_id": "chunk_010-001", "topic": "short topic label", "target": "<the single suggested_target shared by all members>", "member_ids": ["B001-004", "B012-002"], "canonical_claim": "merged claim, union of all specifics, losing none", "issue_ids": ["B140"], "sources": ["path#anchor", "path#anchor"]}

Rules:
- cluster_id: "chunk_010-NNN" with NNN a zero-padded 3-digit sequence starting at 001,
  unique within this file.
- target: must be exactly the `suggested_target` value shared by every member record
  (they must all match — this is why records with different suggested_target can never
  share a cluster).
- member_ids: union of the `id` fields of every record folded into this cluster.
- issue_ids: union of all members' issue_ids (deduplicated).
- sources: union of all members' sources (deduplicated).
- canonical_claim: a single self-contained sentence or short paragraph. When merging
  multiple members, it must preserve every distinct identifier, setting name, number,
  path, and fact from each member claim — do not summarize away specifics.
- Never pretty-print; each output line is exactly one JSON object.

After the JSONL, write /home/mfilimonov/workspace/ClickHouse/master/docs/superpowers/cas/consolidation-2026-08/clusters/chunk_010.clusters.jsonl.manifest with exactly one line:

records:<N> clusters:<M>

where N is the count of input records and M is the count of output cluster lines.
